:["alignment:49e52996069a58a4ed60bc4b"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 125","reason":"For cube side s, the volume loss is s³ - s(s+1)(s-1) = s³ - s(s²-1) = s. Thus s = 5 and the original volume is 5³ = 125. The new volume is 6 × 4 × 5 = 120.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p162"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_10A_Q11","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p160","cnm_p162","cnm_p035"],"id":"solution:base-area-dissection:512f8bf63351","label":"Compare the base areas","methodDirectNodeIds":{"base-area-dissection":["cnm_p163","cnm_p150","cnm_p089"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p163","cnm_p150","cnm_p089","cnm_p160","cnm_p162","cnm_p035"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p160","cnm_p162","cnm_p145","cnm_033"],"id":"solution:volume-difference-equation:512f8bf63351","label":"Compare the volume formulas","methodDirectNodeIds":{"volume-difference-equation":["cnm_p163","cnm_p146","cnm_147","cnm_145","cnm_034"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p163","cnm_p146","cnm_147","cnm_145","cnm_034","cnm_p160","cnm_p162","cnm_p145","cnm_033"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"alignmentIds":["alignment:49e52996069a58a4ed60bc4b"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 864 ft","reason":"For an edge s feet long, volume is s³ cubic feet and surface area is 6(12s)² = 864s² square inches. Since s > 0, s³ = 864s² gives s = 864.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p162"],"coverage":"partial","flags":["The equality is between numerical measurements in different units, not an equality between a volume quantity and an area quantity."],"questionId":"1972_AMC_12_Q12","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_040","cnm_p160","cnm_p089","cnm_p162"],"id":"feet-edge-and-inch-faces","label":"Express each measurement in its stated units","methodDirectNodeIds":{"feet-edge-and-inch-faces":["math:foot-inch-unit-conversion","cnm_p163","cnm_p161"]},"nodeIds":["math:foot-inch-unit-conversion","cnm_p163","cnm_p161","cnm_040","cnm_p160","cnm_p089","cnm_p162"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"alignmentIds":["alignment:49e52996069a58a4ed60bc4b"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: √(2160/π) cm","reason":"The liquid volume is 6 × 3 × 12 = 216 cm³. Thus 0.1πr² = 216, giving r² = 2160/π and r = √(2160/π).","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p162"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"1991_AMC_12_Q08","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p162","cnm_p192","cnm_p206","cnm_074"],"id":"preserve-volume","label":"Equate the two volumes","methodDirectNodeIds":{"preserve-volume":["cnm_p163","cnm_p207","cnm_220"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p163","cnm_p207","cnm_220","cnm_p162","cnm_p192","cnm_p206","cnm_074"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":12,"alignmentIds":["alignment:49e52996069a58a4ed60bc4b"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, (3+√5)/2","reason":"Let R>r>0 be the bottom and top base radii and s the insphere radius. The axial section is an isosceles trapezoid circumscribed about a circle of radius s, with height2s. Equal tangent segments from its four corners show each sloping leg has length R+r. Its horizontal offset is R-r, so Pythagoras gives (R+r)^2=(R-r)^2+4s^2 and s^2=Rr. Extend to the full cone: similarity gives the small/full cone radius ratio r/R and corresponding height ratio; subtract their cone volumes to obtain V_frustum=(pi*(2s)/3)*(R^2+Rr+r^2). The exact sphere formula gives V_sphere=4*pi*s^3/3. The stated volume comparison reduces to R^2+Rr+r^2=4s^2=4Rr, so k=R/r satisfies k^2-3k+1=0. The quadratic root above 1 is (3+sqrt(5))/2, E. Both figures and the text supply an insphere tangent to both bases and the cone side; no diagram scale is used.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p162"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2014_AMC_10B_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h106","cnm_p162","c